    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle v_{\text{S}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/45d7409746d6bce36ba7e6a3a804cdad032b54c7" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:2.274ex; height:2.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle v_{\text{S}}}"></span> are the <a href="/wiki/Molar_volume" title="Molar volume">molar volumes</a> of the liquid and solid phases, and <span class="mwe-math-element"><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"  alttext="{\displaystyle L_{\text{f}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>L</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mtext>f</mtext>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
